    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541617/nutrition-educator-efnep-palm-beach-county": {
      "title": "Nutrition Educator - EFNEP Palm Beach County",
      "description": "Nutrition Educator - EFNEP Palm Beach County Apply now Job no: 541617 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Palm Beach Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Veteran's Preference Eligible Department: 60450000 - AG-EXPANDED NUTRITION PROGRAM Classification Title: Extension Program Ast Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent. Job Description: Program Delivery Promotes EFNEP and recruits eligible youth and adult participants through community outreach and partnerships. Develops and maintains positive working relationships with community organizations to coordinate nutrition education programs, communicate program expectations, and support participant success. Deliver engaging, learner-centered, nutrition education using approved, evidence-based curricula that are responsive to participants’ age, culture, language, literacy level, and learning needs. Delivers instruction through a structured curriculum consisting of a minimum of six lessons for each participant group to promote lasting behavior change. Collects required participant information and administers approved evaluation tools to measure program participation, knowledge gain, and behavior change while maintaining participant confidentiality. Connects participants with Extension programs, community resources, and public assistance programs, including SNAP, when appropriate. Represents EFNEP at health fairs, community events, and outreach activities to increase program awareness, strengthen partnerships, and recruit participants. Planning Plans and coordinates nutrition education programs by scheduling classes with community partners, organizing instructional materials, supplies and equipment, and ensuring classroom logistics support successful program delivery. Adapts activities to meet participant needs while maintaining fidelity to approved curricula and compliance with program requirements. Training Participates in orientation, required trainings, and ongoing professional development to strengthen nutrition knowledge, teaching practices, cultural responsiveness, technology skills, and program implementation. Applies supervisor feedback and new learning to improve program quality and participant outcomes. Travel Travels throughout the assigned county to conduct nutrition education programs, recruit participants, and participate in required meetings and trainings. Occasional overnight travel is required for annual statewide training. Reporting Maintains accurate and timely participant, program, travel, and administrative records in accordance with University, EFNEP, and USDA NIFA requirements. Submits required reports and documentation by established deadlines and protects participant confidentiality. Other duties as assigned. Nutrition Educator will achieve and maintain food safety certification (SafeStaff). Normal work schedule: 40 hours per week, Monday through Friday, 8am-5pm. Required work on nights and weekends when assigned due to the nature of the program. Attachment: EFNEP Core Values.pdf Expected Salary: $19.20 per hour The University of Florida offers highly competitive benefits and retirement options, generous leave plans, a health and wellness program that reflects its commitment to qualify of work, and many more competitive perks and rewards. Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent. Valid Driver's License Preferred: Experience delivering nutrition education, health education, or other educational programming. Experience working with individuals, families, or youth from different backgrounds, particularly with limited resources. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with different audiences. Experience using Microsoft Office applications, Microsoft Teams, Zoom, and other educational technologies. Demonstrates professionalism, adaptability, strong interpersonal skills, and the ability to work independently and collaboratively. Demonstrates effective time management and organizational skills. Comfortable speaking with individuals and groups in both in-person and virtual settings. Ability to lift and carry teaching materials and/or supplies weighing up to 45 pounds. Must be able to stand for extended periods of time indoors and outdoors while delivering lessons. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter, resume and references. This is a time-limited grant funded position in EFNEP Palm Beach County at 559 Military Trail, West Palm Beach, FL 33415. This position is eligible for veteran’s preference. If you are claiming veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 28 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
