tation, required trainings, and ongoing professional development to strengthen nutrition knowledge, teaching practices, cultural responsiveness, technology skills, and program implementation. Applies supervisor feedback and new learning to improve program quality and participant outcomes. Travel Travels throughout the assigned county to conduct nutrition education programs, recruit participants, and participate in required meetings and trainings. Occasional overnight travel is required for annual statewide training. Reporting Maintains accurate and timely participant, program, travel, and administrative records in accordance with University, EFNEP, and USDA NIFA requirements. Submits required reports and documentation by established deadlines and protects participant confidentiality. Other duties as assigned. Nutrition Educator will achieve and maintain food safety certification (SafeStaff). Normal work schedule: 40 hours per week, Monday through Friday, 8am-5pm. Required work on nights and weekends when assigned due to the nature of the program. Criminal Background check required. Attachment: EFNEP Core Values.pdf Expected Salary: $19.20 per hour The University of Florida offers highly competitive benefits and retirement options, generous leave plans, a health and wellness program that reflects its commitment to qualify of work, and many more competitive perks and rewards. Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent Valid driver’s license and reliable daily transportation Preferred: Background in nutrition, and health education, or a related field Demonstrated ability to teach and facilitate group learning Strong public speaking and presentation skills Ability to work with adults and youth in the community Knowledge of local community and its available resources Experience with food preparation, cooking demonstrations, or food safety Working knowledge of MS Office programs (Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint, etc.) Bilingual (English/Spanish) Demonstrates professionalism, adaptability, strong interpersonal skills, and the ability to work independently and collaboratively. Demonstrates effective time management and organizational skills. Comfortable speaking with individuals and groups in both in-person and virtual settings. Ability to lift and carry teaching materials and/or supplies weighing up to 45 pounds. Must be able to stand for extended periods of time indoors and outdoors while delivering lessons. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter, resume and references. This is a time-limited, grant funded position in EFNEP Escambia County Extension at 3740 Stefani Road, Cantonment, FL 32533. This position is eligible for veteran’s preference. If you are claiming veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 28 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
