    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541621/director-of-development-strategic-alumni-engagement": {
      "title": "Director of Development & Strategic Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Director of Development & Strategic Alumni Engagement Apply now Job no: 541621 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Advancement Department: 31010100 - NR-DEAN-ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: Director of Development & Strategic Alumni Engagement Classification Minimum Requirements: Masters degree in appropriate area of specialization and three years of appropriate experience in Development or a related field; or a bachelors degree in appropriate areas of specialization and five years of experience in Development or a related field. Job Description: Portfolio Management Manage and strategically grow a portfolio of major gift prospects donors (rated from $100,000 and above). Responsible for identifying and building relationships with prospects through face-to-face visits and developing cultivation strategies. Develop and execute individualized cultivation and solicitation strategies aligned with college funding priorities. Partner with faculty and college leadership to align donor interests with institutional initiatives. Identify and develop relationships with private, family and corporate foundations whose philanthropic priorities align with college initiatives; coordinate strategy, proposal development, cultivation, stewardship, and reporting in partnerships with college leadership and UF Advancement. Develop and execute a comprehensive engagement and programming strategy that advances the College’s priorities across its s ix key stakeholder audiences: alumni, donors, students, parents/families, faculty/staff, and corporate/community partners. Partner with the College’s corporate relations leadership to identify, research, qualify, and prioritize corporations and corporate foundations whose philanthropic, workforce, talent, community engagement, or strategic priorities align with the College of Nursing. Manage Dean’s Circle of Excellence, including solicitation and stewardship of members. Coordinate major gift outreach activities, including stewardship. Record and manage all donor activity within the Advance database; ensure accurate prospect tracking and pipeline management. Analyze giving trends and prepare strategic reports and presentations for leadership. Proactively identify new major gift and planned giving prospects through research and strategic engagement efforts. Alumni Affairs Efforts Identify, develop, pilot and evaluate new approaches to alumni engagement and donor experience using constituent insights and data. Establish new programs to engage alumni with faculty and students. Track, measures and reports on all alumni engagement activities. Partner with communications staff to oversee alumni-facing communications (website, social media, newsletters, email, and video content). Plan and produces select alumni engagement events. Work closely with UF Alumni Relations staff to coordinate alumni affairs efforts across UF. Event Strategy & Donor Stewardship Assist in identifying award recipients for annual donor recognition event and Dorothy M. Smith Leadership Awards. Work with Senior Director on script and presentation for the Donor Recognition Event. Support the strategic planning and execution of donor recognition and stewardship events, including the annual Donor Recognition Event and leadership award programs. Serve as a host and advancement representative at college and university events. Oversee pre- and post-event donor engagement and follow-up communications. Collaborate on the design and development of event collateral, pledge materials, and stewardship communications. Participate in university events and serve on volunteer committees as needed. Work with Development Coordinator on scholarship Thank You notes for donors. Connect alumni, cultivation, recognition, and stewardship events to broader advancement objectives through defined audiences, relationship goals, pre-event strategy, post-event follow up, and appropriate measures of success. Quality Assurance Ensure best practices in office systems, files and record keeping. Ensure effective use of strategic tools and resources such as contact reports, prospect management, research and analysis, and the Advance database. Plan and monitor the budget, using resources for best results in fundraising and planning activities involving volunteers, prospects, faculty, and administration. Expected Salary: Commensurate with education and experience Required Qualifications: Masters degree in appropriate area of specialization and three years of appropriate experience in Development or a related field; or a bachelors degree in appropriate areas of specialization and five years of experience in Development or a related field. Valid Drivers License is required. Preferred: Three to five years of major gift fundraising experience with proven success soliciting gifts of $25,000 and above strongly preferred. Related experience working with volunteers and/or in similar organization. Enthusiasm for fundraising in a comprehensive research university and the desire to work collegially within a goal-oriented fundraising organization. Knowledge of fundraising principles, methods, and standards. Expertise in developing solicitation strategies. The ability to work strategically, develop and implement constituency programs and activities, along with a talent for motivating volunteers. Ability to work collaboratively and as a team player Competency in problem solving. Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, strong interpersonal abilities, and the capacity to engage effectively and collaboratively with a wide range of individuals are essential. Support the University’s commitment to creating a respectful and collaborative work environment that values integrity, professionalism, and mutual respect in all interactions; demonstrated success collaborating with stakeholders; strong project management skills; experience in a data-driven environment; excellent organizational abilities; and the capacity to lead, influence, and inspire others are essential. Proficient in the following areas: Windows operating systems, Microsoft Word, Excel, and Access, as well as internet browsers and email platforms. Familiarity with donor databases, contact management systems, and tracking systems is also highly preferred. The ability and willingness to travel. A valid driver license and good driving record are essential.* Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 20 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541622/insurance-office-clinical-service-rep-ii-revenue-cycle-specialist": {
      "title": "Insurance Office Clinical Service Rep II (Revenue Cycle Specialist)",
      "description": "Insurance Office Clinical Service Rep II (Revenue Cycle Specialist) Apply now Job no: 541622 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Veteran's Preference Eligible, Health Care Administration/Support Department: 35010204 - SH-INSURANCE OFFICE Classification Title: Clin Service Representative II Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent and two years of relevant office experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute an equivalent rate for the required experience. Job Description: The Opportunity The Student Health Care Center (SHCC) at the University of Florida is seeking two Clinical Service Representative II (Revenue Cycle Specialist) positions. Reporting to the Coding and Reimbursement Supervisor, you’ll play a key role in supporting the billing and reimbursement process while helping students access and understand healthcare services. The key responsibilities of the position include the following: Financial Support Facilitating established financial processes that enable and expedite the billing and collection of professional services. This includes entering charges, applying basic coding/billing rules, maximizing collections, verifying insurance, obtaining authorizations for services, reviewing patient account details, and financial counseling of patients. Accountable for resolving front-end edits, rejections, and information requests to achieve practice goals. EHR Support Responsible for reviewing and updating patient account details and entering and verifying insurance. Obtain all consent forms, copies of identification/ insurance cards, and other required documentation. Verify student status/eligibility for services and select the appropriate guarantor for appointment. Ensures scanning of paper documents in EPIC is properly completed, labeled, and placed in the correct tab of the patient EHR. Work effectively with a wide range of students whose needs may be difficult to assess on initial contact. Responsible for posting insurance and patient payments accurately and efficiently. Monitor claims through the reimbursement process and follow up on outstanding claims. Investigate and resolve claim denials, rejections, and underpayments. Submit appeals and supporting documentation to insurance carriers as needed. Communicate with insurance companies to resolve claim and payment issues. Maintain accurate billing records and documentation. Assist patients with billing questions, payment processing, and balance inquiries. Collaborate with providers and staff to support accurate charge capture and reimbursement Denied Claims Troubleshooting, researching, and making corrections to ensure claims are clean and reprocessed for payment or written off when not eligible for payment. Payment posting Assist with insurance updates in the EPIC system at the beginning of each quarter. Serve as in-house insurance educator for support staff and assist with questions on the insurance process and application in the EPIC system. Typical Schedule: 8 am to 5 pm daily (Monday through Friday) and one-hour lunch during Fall and Spring semesters. 8 am to 4:30 pm daily (Monday through Friday) with a one-half hour lunch during Summer semesters. The Opportunity The Student Health Care Center (SHCC) at the University of Florida is seeking two Clinical Service Representative II (Revenue Cycle Specialist) positions. Reporting to the Coding and Reimbursement Supervisor, you’ll play a key role in supporting the billing and reimbursement process while helping students access and understand healthcare services. The key responsibilities of the position include the following: Financial Support Facilitating established financial processes that enable and expedite the billing and collection of professional services. This includes entering charges, applying basic coding/billing rules, maximizing collections, verifying insurance, obtaining authorizations for services, reviewing patient account details, and financial counseling of patients. Accountable for resolving front-end edits, rejections, and information requests to achieve practice goals. EHR Support Responsible for reviewing and updating patient account details and entering and verifying insurance. Obtain all consent forms, copies of identification/ insurance cards, and other required documentation. Verify student status/eligibility for services and select the appropriate guarantor for appointment. Ensures scanning of paper documents in EPIC is properly completed, labeled, and placed in the correct tab of the patient EHR. Work effectively with a wide range of students whose needs may be difficult to assess on initial contact. Responsible for posting insurance and patient payments accurately and efficiently. Monitor claims through the reimbursement process and follow up on outstanding claims. Investigate and resolve claim denials, rejections, and underpayments. Submit appeals and supporting documentation to insurance carriers as needed. Communicate with insurance companies to resolve claim and payment issues. Maintain accurate billing records and documentation. Assist patients with billing questions, payment processing, and balance inquiries. Collaborate with providers and staff to support accurate charge capture and reimbursement Denied Claims Troubleshooting, researching, and making corrections to ensure claims are clean and reprocessed for payment or written off when not eligible for payment. Payment posting Assist with insurance updates in the EPIC system at the beginning of each quarter. Serve as in-house insurance educator for support staff and assist with questions on the insurance process and application in the EPIC system. Typical Schedule: • 8 am to 5 pm daily (Monday through Friday) and one-hour lunch during Fall and Spring semesters. • 8 am to 4:30 pm daily (Monday through Friday) with a one-half hour lunch during Summer semesters. About the Student Health Care Center (SHCC) The mission of the SHCC is to help every student achieve optimal health in pursuing personal and academic success. Our vision is to be the preferred healthcare provider for University of Florida students as a nationally recognized leader in the collegiate health specialty. The SHCC is fully accredited by the AAAHC and is located in a state-of-the-art WELL-certified building on UF’s campus. Medical services offered at the SHCC include primary care, sports medicine, urgent care, gynecology, psychiatry, allergy/immunization clinic, and travel medicine. Radiology, pharmacy, lab, and physical therapy are also on site. Learn more about SHCC here https://shcc.ufl.edu/ About the University of Florida UF is one of the nation’s top universities and a dynamic and rewarding place to work. UF is in Gainesville, one of Florida’s most livable cities. Known for its natural attractions (wetlands, forests, springs, wildlife) and cultural offerings (music, theater, visual arts, and historic districts), the area also is gaining a reputation as a thriving hub for high-tech start-ups, as well as invention and research collaborations. We are excited about what’s happening here and know you will want to be a part of it. The City of Gainesville The Guide to Greater Gainesville shares all that you need to learn about the Heart of Florida, including neighborhood and city information, schools and zoning, culture and leisure, sports and fitness, healthcare and much more. Learn more at https://guidetogreatergainesville.com/ Expected Salary: $20.00-$22.00 per hour Exclusive Perks and Benefits Enjoy stability and support with UF’s unique range of benefits and opportunities. With a robust healthcare package, generous leave policies, retirement planning, and professional development , you can achieve a healthy work-life balance, plan for your future, and advance your career. Full-time TEAMS employees will accrue vacation leave at a rate of 6.769 hours biweekly/22 days annually and sick leave at a rate of 4 hours biweekly/13 days annually. In addition, employees are eligible for ten paid holidays each year. Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and two years of relevant office experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute an equivalent rate for the required experience. Preferred: EXPERIENCE: Experience with computer programs for word processing and various computer software applications Experience with computer-generated appointment systems and EHR KNOWLEDGE: Understanding of insurance plans, terms Ability to interpret Explanation of Benefits EPIC system knowledge and experience Understanding of Bursar file systems Knowledge of CPT, HCPCS, and ICD-10 Working knowledge of WayStar and Availity SKILLS: Organizational Verbal and written communication Math Leadership Customer Service Oriented ABILITIES: Concentration Ability to work independently Ability to organize and maintain patient records Ability to plan, organize, and coordinate work assignments Ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing Ability to evaluate problems and implement solutions Ability to compile and analyze data for administrative decisions Work independently using good judgment in establishing and maintaining office procedures and routines OTHER QUALIFICATIONS: Friendly Ability to work independently Ability to organize and maintain patient records Ability to plan, organize, and coordinate work assignments Ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing Ability to evaluate problems and implement solutions Ability to compile and analyze data for administrative decisions Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter, resume, and a list of at least 3 references. Applications must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 20 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541623/nutrition-educator-efnep-miamidade-county": {
      "title": "Nutrition Educator - EFNEP Miami-Dade County",
      "description": "Nutrition Educator - EFNEP Miami-Dade County Apply now Job no: 541623 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Dade Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Veteran's Preference Eligible Department: 60450000 - AG-EXPANDED NUTRITION PROGRAM Classification Title: Extension Program Ast Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent. Job Description: Program Delivery Promotes EFNEP and recruits eligible youth and adult participants through community outreach and partnerships. Develops and maintains positive working relationships with community organizations to coordinate nutrition education programs, communicate program expectations, and support participant success. Deliver engaging, learner-centered, nutrition education using approved, evidence-based curricula that are responsive to participants’ age, culture, language, literacy level, and learning needs. Delivers instruction through a structured curriculum consisting of a minimum of six lessons for each participant group to promote lasting behavior change. Collects required participant information and administers approved evaluation tools to measure program participation, knowledge gain, and behavior change while maintaining participant confidentiality. Connects participants with Extension programs, community resources, and public assistance programs, including SNAP, when appropriate. Represents EFNEP at health fairs, community events, and outreach activities to increase program awareness, strengthen partnerships, and recruit participants. Planning Plans and coordinates nutrition education programs by scheduling classes with community partners, organizing instructional materials, supplies and equipment, and ensuring classroom logistics support successful program delivery. Adapts activities to meet participant needs while maintaining fidelity to approved curricula and compliance with program requirements. Training Participates in orientation, required trainings, and ongoing professional development to strengthen nutrition knowledge, teaching practices, cultural responsiveness, technology skills, and program implementation. Applies supervisor feedback and new learning to improve program quality and participant outcomes. Travel Travels throughout the assigned county to conduct nutrition education programs, recruit participants, and participate in required meetings and trainings. Occasional overnight travel is required for annual statewide training. Reporting Maintains accurate and timely participant, program, travel, and administrative records in accordance with University, EFNEP, and USDA NIFA requirements. Submits required reports and documentation by established deadlines and protects participant confidentiality. Other duties as assigned. Nutrition Educator will achieve and maintain food safety certification (SafeStaff). Normal work schedule: 40 hours per week, Monday through Friday, 8am-5pm. Required work on nights and weekends when assigned due to the nature of the program. Criminal background check required. Attachment: EFNEP Core Values.pdf Expected Salary: $19.20 per hour The University of Florida offers highly competitive benefits and retirement options, generous leave plans, a health and wellness program that reflects its commitment to qualify of work, and many more competitive perks and rewards. Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent Valid driver's license and reliable daily transportation Preferred: Background in nutrition, health education, or a related field Demonstrated ability to teach and facilitate group learning Strong public speaking and presentation skills Experience working with adults, youth, or limited-resource clients Working knowledge of MS Office programs (Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint, etc.) Bilingual (English/Spanish) Demonstrates professionalism, adaptability, strong interpersonal skills, and the ability to work independently and collaboratively. Demonstrates effective time management and organizational skills. Comfortable speaking with individuals and groups in both in-person and virtual settings. Ability to lift and carry teaching materials and/or supplies weighing up to 45 pounds. Must be able to stand for extended periods of time indoors and outdoors while delivering lessons. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter, resume and references. This is a time-limited, grant funded position in EFNEP Miami-Dade County at 14400 NW 77th CT, Suite 106, Miami Lakes, FL 33016 Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. We are hiring two Nutrition Educators through this posting. This position is eligible for veteran’s preference. If you are claiming veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 28 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541624/assistant-professor-in-bands": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Bands",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Bands Apply now Job no: 541624 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Humanities Department: 13030200 - COTA-BANDS Classification Title: AST PROF Classification Minimum Requirements Candidates for this rank shall hold the highest degree appropriate to their field or possess equivalent qualifications based on professional experience. A candidate shall be expected to demonstrate successful experience pertinent to the position they are being recommended and have demonstrated qualities relevant to the goals of the academic unit in which they will be employed. Job Description: The University of Florida School of Music in the College of the Arts invites applications for a full-time, 9-month Assistant Professor in the Bands area with an appointment starting August 16, 2027. We seek an accomplished pedagogue who will contribute to the continued success and growth of a comprehensive band program. The successful candidate will instruct concert and athletic ensembles, bringing a dynamic personality and enthusiasm for teaching to our existing community of outstanding scholars and musicians. The University of Florida College of the Arts intends to be a transformative community, responding to and generating paradigmatic shifts in the arts and beyond. As artists and scholars, we embrace the complexity of our evolving human experience and seek to empower our students and faculty to shape that experience fearlessly through critical study, creative practice, and provocation. We seek a colleague who identifies as a change-maker. We seek a colleague who will position emerging artists and researchers as catalysts for justice on local and global levels. This position is covered by the United Faculty of Florida Contract. You can view this employment union contract here https://admin.hr.ufl.edu/compliance/employee-relations-and-ethics/union-negotiations/united-faculty-of-florida-contract/ . Responsibilities: Tenure Accruing Responsibilities • Collaborate with the Director of Bands and Associate Director of Bands in the day-to-day operations of the band program, ensuring effective rehearsals, performances, and administrative coordination. • Assist with the planning, preparation, and execution of performances, including concerts, athletic events, tours, and special programs. • Conduct and rehearse assigned concert bands, athletic bands, and related ensembles in support of the artistic and educational mission of the band program. • Teach undergraduate conducting courses. • Collaborate with band faculty and staff on scheduling, equipment coordination, and ensemble logistics. • Support recruitment, retention, and outreach activities for the band program and School of Music. • Participate in service activities appropriate to a tenure-accruing faculty appointment, including faculty meetings and School of Music events. • Perform additional duties as assigned in support of the mission and goals of the band program and School of Music. Summer Faculty Appointment Responsibilities • Beginning on the first day of each Summer B session and continuing through the start of Fall classes, assist with planning and preparations for the band program. SCHOOL OF MUSIC: Organized within the College of the Arts, the School of Music plays an important role in the academic and cultural life of the University, the College’s Creative Campus initiative and the community. The School has 40 full-time and nine adjunct faculty, serving some 200 graduate and 200 undergraduate music majors. Degree programs include B.S., B.A., B.M., M.M., D.M.A., and the Ph.D. in music education, composition, ethnomusicology, and historical musicology. Program emphases include performance, music education, theory, composition, music history and literature, ethnomusicology, conducting, and sacred music. The School of Music is also home to the UF Bands program, which includes “The Pride of the Sunshine” Gator Marching Band. School of Music facilities include the School of Music Building and Steinbrenner Band Hall, among others. The University of Florida is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges and is an accredited institutional member of the National Association of Schools of Music. For more information, visit www.arts.ufl.edu/music . THE COLLEGE OF THE ARTS: The College of the Arts is an engine of transformation that generates paradigmatic shifts in the arts and beyond, while nurturing adaptability, innovation, and excellence. We foster an environment where novel creative practice, leading research, and experiential learning thrive. Our students, faculty, and staff interrogate and respond to the ever-changing relationship between technology and the human spirit. We prepare future leaders in artistic professions and creative industries, while developing student capacity for interdisciplinary scholarship that serves and engages local and global communities. The College offers baccalaureate, masters, and doctoral degrees. Approximately 1,600 students are pursuing majors in degrees offered by the College of the Arts under the direction of 150 faculty members in its three accredited schools— the School of Art + Art History, the School of Music, and the School of Theatre + Dance, and in the Center for Arts in Medicine, the Digital Worlds Institute, and the Center for Arts, Migration, and Entrepreneurship. In addition, the college comprises the University Galleries, and the University level of the New World School of the Arts in Miami. The University of Florida: The University of Florida is a comprehensive learning institution built on a land grant foundation. We are The Gator Nation, a community dedicated to excellence in education and research and shaping a better future for Florida, the nation and the world. Our mission is to enable our students to lead and influence the next generation and beyond for economic, cultural and societal benefit. UF is a graduate research institution with more than 50,000 students and membership in the prestigious Association of American Universities. Gainesville, which is consistently ranked as one of the nation’s most livable cities, is located midway between the Gulf of Mexico and the Atlantic Ocean. Together, the University and the community comprise the educational, medical and cultural center of North Central Florida. In addition to salary, the University of Florida (UF) offers low cost State Health plans, a number of Dental plans to fit you and your family’s needs, and Vision. Domestic partner coverage through GatorCare is also available. Optional plans such as life, disability, legal and accident insurance are also available. UF provides a variety of leave programs including vacation, sick leave, 11 paid holidays, personal leave days, and family medical leave. Nine-month faculty employees accrue approximately 13 sick days annually, and 4 personal leave days, typically used during the holiday closing period (accruals based on full-time employment). UF also provides you the flexibility to deal with life’s challenges by offering paid family leave, eight full weeks of leave over a 24-month period. Build a retirement roadmap with competitive pension plans, investment accounts and a host of voluntary add-ons, such as 457 deferred compensation and 403(b) plans. UF Employees are also eligible for the GatorPerks discount program , which provides big savings at various business and retailers! Explore UF’s plethora of benefit options here: FACULTY Benefits Expected Salary: Assistant Professor: $61,000-$63,000 based on qualifications and experience with a comprehensive and highly competitive leave and benefits package Summer Faculty appointment: $5,000-$6,000 Required Qualifications: The successful candidate must meet all the following Doctorate or ABD in music (Instrumental Conducting or Music Education) Evidence of successful music teaching experience in instrumental music (concert and athletic bands) at the collegiate and/or high school level Evidence of success in marching band drill design and/or music arranging Evidence of successful collaboration and collegiality with faculty, students, and staff Evidence of skill in designing and facilitating academic work that advances curiosity, respect, open intellectual discourse, and the welcome incorporation and well-being of all in an environment of complex differences. Preferred The successful candidate will meet some of the following Teaching experience of 3 to 5 years beyond graduate assistantship at the university level Expertise in marching band drill design and/or music arranging Demonstrated capacity for effective engagement in recruiting Organizational, management, and communication experience within higher education Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin November 16, 2026, and continue until an applicant pool is established. To ensure full consideration, all application documents must be submitted by November 16, 2026. Applications received after this date may be considered at the discretion of the committee and/or hiring authority. Application Process: Applications must be submitted via the University of Florida’s online application system. Online applications must include the following: (1) A detailed letter of application that explains how you match the particular qualifications of this position and how your work and perspective will contribute to and enhance our transformative community; (2) A curriculum vitae; (3) A document containing links to 20-30 minutes of conducting footage that shows both rehearsal and performance (4) Names and contact information for three professional references. (5) Submit name and contact information for a staff or administrative member that we may contact for a phone conversation. The UF system will give you the option to upload letters of reference. We are not requiring letters of reference with initial application materials. Please ignore that option. The Search Committee may request additional materials at a later time. Inquiries may be sent to: Chip Birkner Chair, Ast Prof in Bands Search chipbirk@ufl.edu Applications will only be removed from consideration after being reviewed by the humans on the search committee. The selected candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES). If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call +1 (352) 392- 2477or the Florida Relay System at +1 (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541625/administrative-assistant-i": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant I",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant I Apply now Job no: 541625 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Veteran's Preference Eligible Department: 11230000 - RE-AI AND INFORMATICS (AIIRI) Classification Title: Administrative Assistant I Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Daily operations support through: fiscal processing, assist with director and assistant director travel booking and processing reimbursement, manage AIIRI email and inquiries made through website form, phone, supply inventory and ordering, maintain office filing systems, interacting with vendors and or service providers for space or service contracts, space maintenance, greeting/guiding visitors to the space, lecture room and conference room calendar management. Assist in event coordination. From space reservations, catering coordination, drafting and assist in editing email, newsletters, and event advertisements, guest travel scheduling/booking, and processing reimbursements. Other special projects as needed by AIIRI Administrative Assistant III or AIIRI Director. Expected Salary: Commensurate with Education and Experience. Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Preferred Experience with UF financial systems and PeopleSoft. Strong knowledge of MS-Office, particularly Word, Excel, and Power Point. Strong communication skills both written and oral. Able to build strong working relationships with others. Special Instructions to Applicants: • In order to be considered, applicants must provide a cover letter, resume, and list of professional references. • Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. • This is not a remote position and is located on the University of Florida main campus in Gainesville, FL. • A criminal background check is required. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 13 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541626/manager-of-administrative-services-department-of-orthopaedics-surgery-and-sports-medicine": {
      "title": "Manager of Administrative Services - Department of Orthopaedics Surgery and Sports Medicine",
      "description": "Manager of Administrative Services - Department of Orthopaedics Surgery and Sports Medicine Apply now Job no: 541626 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Health Care Administration/Support Department: 29170000 - MD-ORTHOPAEDICS - REHAB Classification Title: Manager, Administrative Services Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area and three years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: The Manager of Administrative Services provides strategic administrative leadership and oversight for the Department of Orthopaedics Surgery and Sports Medicine, ensuring effective coordination and delivery of administrative functions, resources, processes, and support services. The position oversees administrative staff; coordinates workforce planning, faculty affairs, recruitment, onboarding, and organizational support; and manages administrative processes to promote efficiency, compliance, accountability, and continuity of services. The Manager partners with departmental leadership to support strategic priorities, strengthen administrative practices, and ensure resources and services are aligned with departmental needs. The Manager serves as a key administrative advisor and liaison to departmental, College of Medicine, University, and health system leadership, coordinating cross-functional activities and supporting effective communication and collaboration. The position develops and implements administrative policies and procedures, evaluates administrative processes, and identifies opportunities to enhance efficiency, service delivery, and resource utilization. Through effective staff leadership, performance management, project coordination, and continuous improvement, the Manager ensures the department has the administrative infrastructure and support necessary to advance its clinical, academic, research, and educational missions. More about this role: Administrative Services and Departmental Management Provide leadership and oversight of departmental administrative services, ensuring alignment with the strategic priorities of the Department Chair, Vice Chair of Administrative Services & Finance, and departmental leadership. Serve as a primary administrative liaison among departmental leadership, University and College of Medicine executives, hospital administration, faculty, and external organizations. Manage complex administrative initiatives, special projects, faculty leadership activities, strategic meetings, and events; develop and monitor project plans, timelines, deliverables, and outcomes. Interpret and implement University, College of Medicine, and departmental policies and procedures while advising faculty, managers, and staff on administrative requirements, compliance, and effective administrative practices. Assess administrative processes and identify opportunities to strengthen coordination, consistency, accountability, and service delivery. Lead administrative personnel, including recruitment, onboarding, performance management, workload distribution, payroll and time approval, leave administration, professional development, and compliance with employment policies. Provide leadership, direction and support for staff development to ensure staff responsibilities and departmental priorities are coordinated effectively and completed in a timely manner. Administrative Services and Professional Organization Management Coordinate and provide administrative support for departmental executive responsibilities associated with local, regional, and national professional organizations, supporting the Department Chair, Vice Chair, Associate Director of Finance, Associate Director of Revenue Cycle, and designated faculty leaders. Manage deadlines, correspondence, submissions, meeting schedules, and follow-up activities to ensure timely completion of organizational responsibilities and effective support of departmental leadership. Develop, coordinate, and maintain executive-level materials for professional society activities, including reports, presentations, agendas, briefing materials, meeting packets, budgets, membership records, correspondence, and organizational documentation. Maintain organized records and administrative resources that support leadership decision-making, institutional knowledge, and continuity of departmental activities. Oversee the coordination of domestic and international travel arrangements in support of departmental leadership and faculty participation in professional, academic, and organizational activities. Manage travel requests and authorizations, conference registrations, airfare and lodging, ground transportation, itineraries, scheduling, expense documentation, reimbursements, and related administrative requirements. Ensure travel documentation is complete and consistent with university policies, applicable funding requirements, and organizational deadlines. Administer administrative tracking and compliance support for professional memberships, medical licensure, CME requirements, certifications, subscriptions, and related renewals. Monitor expiration dates and required actions, initiate renewal and documentation requests, maintain centralized records, and provide timely reminders and administrative support to help ensure continued compliance with professional and organizational requirements. Administrative Coordination and Clinical Services Support Coordinate administrative activities between UF Orthopaedics and the University Athletic Association to support timely access to orthopedic care for students and athletes. Facilitate communication and administrative coordination among providers, patients, athletic staff, and clinical personnel. Coordinate administrative arrangements related to consultations, diagnostic testing, specialty referrals, imaging, laboratory services, and multidisciplinary appointments. Maintain appropriate documentation and facilitate timely communication and follow-up among relevant stakeholders. Compile, organize, and report sports health-related administrative and service data to support departmental planning, quality initiatives, leadership reporting, and informed decision-making. Faculty Affairs and Development Manage administrative support for the department's faculty development and academic advancement programs in collaboration with departmental leadership. Coordinate faculty promotion and tenure activities, annual evaluations, Faculty Evaluation and Advancement (FEA) processes, Faculty Activity and Achievement Reporting (FAAR), effort reporting, and related institutional reporting requirements. Monitor established timelines, coordinate required documentation, maintain records, and ensure alignment with College of Medicine and University requirements. Prepare reports, status updates, and administrative materials for departmental leadership regarding faculty development and advancement activities. Identify opportunities to strengthen administrative support, consistency, and communication related to faculty affairs. Faculty Recruitment Administration Manage the administrative coordination of faculty recruitment activities for clinical and research positions from position approval through onboarding. Coordinate recruitment activities in collaboration with departmental leadership, search committees, Human Resources, and other institutional stakeholders. Oversee position postings, applicant tracking, interview scheduling, recruitment communications, candidate travel arrangements, search committee materials, employment documentation, onboarding, and transition activities. Maintain accurate recruitment records, monitor established timelines, prepare status reports for leadership, and ensure recruitment activities are administered in accordance with university policies and procedures. Administrative Leadership Provide administrative leadership and support to departmental executives through coordination with the Dean's Office, College of Medicine leadership, hospital administration, division chiefs, faculty, and external stakeholders. Serve as a key administrative resource to facilitate communication, coordination, and follow-through on departmental priorities and leadership initiatives. Provide oversight and direction to staff responsible for faculty clinical calendar and scheduling support. Coordinate presentations, reports, strategic meetings, leadership materials, and special initiatives while exercising independent judgment, maintaining confidentiality, and ensuring timely completion of assigned responsibilities. Develop and maintain administrative processes, resources, and support structures that promote consistent service delivery, effective communication, accountability, and organizational effectiveness. Provide administrative support to departmental Vice Chairs, Associate Directors, and Sports Medicine leadership as needed. Ensure appropriate administrative coverage, mentor and support administrative staff, and perform related managerial responsibilities as assigned. Expected Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area and three years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in a healthcare setting Familiarity with the role of the Chair of the department and Executive Director, to provide professional-level assistance effectively/proactively Familiarity with collecting and preparing data analyses Proficiency in Microsoft Office, including Outlook, Excel, and PowerPoint Demonstrate project management skills Ability to compose own correspondence and edit/proofread that of others Capable of working under pressure and producing within deadlines Ability to prioritize own work and proceed with minimum supervision Ability to maintain a professional approach at all times Demonstrate ease with learning new programs Maintains strict confidentiality at all times Interacts professionally with the public in a sensitive and professional manner; screens requests and materials effectively and efficiently; and readily handles a variety of situations Works independently and as a team member Highly organized and consistently demonstrates personal initiative Displays interest in the overall well-being of the health system Takes initiative to assist whenever possible in the success of the institution Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 13 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541627/director-faculty-rank-tbd": {
      "title": "Director & Faculty (Rank TBD)",
      "description": "Director & Faculty (Rank TBD) Apply now Job no: 541627 Work type: Faculty Admin Title Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Engineering Department: 19010520 - EG-LEADERSHIP PROGRAMS Classification Title: Director & Faculty (Rank TBD) Classification Minimum Requirements: • Master’s degree in engineering • Experience in successfully leading organizations (industry and/or academic) and partnering with external advisory boards • Experience in successful stakeholder engagement activities (external and internal), including nurturing donor relationships and fundraising • Maintains key personal qualities as a good communicator with good presence and high energy Job Description: ELI, located in the UF Wertheim Laboratory for Engineering Excellence , offers both undergraduate and graduate coursework and certificate programs in engineering leadership, engineering project management, and engineering and AI ethics and safety. Since its inception in 2011, over 16,000 students have completed coursework in ELI and almost 1,000 students have graduated with earned academic certificate credentials in engineering leadership or engineering project management. With three other permanent staff, dedicated adjunct instructors (many of whom are practicing engineers), a committed Advisory Board, faculty fellows, affiliates and partners, and shared support of the core values and expectations of ELI faculty and students , ELI is now poised to further enrich the education of engineering students through new academic programs, enhanced engagement programming for current and former students, and educational outreach to external partners. The responsibilities of the ELI Director include but are not limited to the following: Ensuring fulfillment of ELI’s vision and mission and regular communication of the vision to internal and external stakeholders. Overseeing curriculum enhancement and the creation of innovative degree initiatives and academic programs through strong collaboration with the HWCOE leadership, ELI Advisory Board, and college/university units and individuals. Ensuring the relevance of all ELI curriculum by evaluation and application of career-readiness competencies, assessment at the course and program levels, and surveying of current and former students and employers. Partnering with HWCOE Advancement officers in developing ELI donor relationships and active fundraising for existing and visioned ELI activities. Leading grant proposal writing and submissions to enhance funding for ELI activities and initiatives. Supporting development and implementation of leadership training programs for external non-UF entities. Closely partnering with the ELI Advisory Board, meeting on a semesterly basis and engaging members in events and other activities. Leading, mentoring, supporting, and building camaraderie among ELI staff, which currently include 3 other permanent faculty members and 14 additional supporting personnel. Performing administrative duties that include reporting to the Florida Board of Governors, UF Office of Institutional Planning and Research, UF Advancement, and the Commission on Colleges and Universities. Serving as a primary contributor in planning ELI events, which include the Linda Parker Hudson Leader-in-Residence Program. Managing the ELI budget and leading fiscal planning activities for ELI. Actively engaging in teaching ELI courses, ideally in the areas of project management, leadership, or professional development for doctoral students. Actively engaging in the American Society of Engineering Education LEADs Division activities. Administering the ELI Faculty Fellows, ELI Partners, and Kirkland Engineering Leadership Professor Programs by selecting participants, holding regular meetings, and intentionally building a coalition of internal and external collaborators who will further the mission of ELI. Collaborating closely with HWCOE partners, including the Engineering Innovation Institute, Department of Engineering Education, faculty throughout HWCOE, and academic advisors, through meetings (as needed) and their participation in ELI events and activities. Meeting regularly with the HWCOE Senior Associate Dean (and Dean) as required. Supporting expansion of extracurricular student programming and alumni outreach activities. Expected Salary: Commensurate with Education and Experience Required Qualifications: • Master’s degree in engineering • Experience in successfully leading organizations (industry and/or academic) and partnering with external advisory boards • Experience in successful stakeholder engagement activities (external and internal), including nurturing donor relationships and fundraising • Maintains key personal qualities as a good communicator with good presence and high energy Preferred: Experience in teaching undergraduate and graduate students Experience in proposal writing and fundraising Experience in building and infusing organizational culture Maintains a program/project manager mentality UF HWCOE graduate Special Instructions to Applicants: The search committee will begin reviewing applications immediately and will continue to review applications until the position is filled. You must apply by submitting an application through UFCareers via https://jobs.ufl.edu/ . (Job 541627 ) The application consists of attached PDF files of the following required documents: 1. Cover letter (summary, introduction related to hiring-emphasis areas) 2. Resume or curriculum vitae (including a 1-page CV highlights) 3. Names, addresses, phone numbers, and email addresses of no less than three and up to five references. Additional documents should be uploaded as one PDF to the “other documents” selection in the application. 4. A personal leadership experience summary detailing previous leadership roles and outcomes achieved. 5. A vision statement for leading ELI into the future, including short- and long-term goals and identifying synergies of these goals with previous leadership-related curriculum and programming activities. 6. A personal leadership philosophy statement. The anticipated start date for this position is January 2, 2027. For further questions, please contact Search Committee Chair and Senior Associate Dean Dr. John Shea at jmshea@ufl.edu or Acting ELI Director, Mr. Bill McElroy, P.E. at mcelrowj@ufl.edu . The University of Florida (UF) is the flagship campus of the State of Florida university system and is consistently ranked among the nation’s top public universities. UF is home to HiPerGator, the fastest AI supercomputer in higher education, and the Herbert Wertheim College of Engineering is undergoing a major expansion in faculty, research, and facilities with a strong focus on artificial intelligence. In Fall 2023, UF opened Malachowsky Hall for Data Science & Information Technology, a 260,000-square-foot facility that serves as the hub for AI. For more information about college initiatives, visit eng.ufl.edu Additional Requirements The selected candidate must provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. Transcripts marked “Issued to Student” will not be considered official. Degrees earned outside the United States must be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES) . Additional Information The University and College count among its greatest strengths a community of faculty, students and staff who support a culture of respect and dignity where learning and research thrive. If you require a reasonable accommodation to apply, please call 352-392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at 800-955-8771 (TDD) . Employment is contingent upon eligibility to work in the United States. All searches are conducted in accordance with Florida’s Sunshine Law . The University of Florida is an equal opportunity employer. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541628/university-registrar-services-coordinator-iii-degree-audit": {
      "title": "University Registrar Services Coordinator III (Degree Audit)",
      "description": "University Registrar Services Coordinator III (Degree Audit) Apply now Job no: 541628 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Student Services Department: 03030000 - EM-OFFICE OF REGISTRAR Classification Title: Univ Registrar Svcs CRD III Classification Minimum Requirements: Master’s degree in an appropriate area; or a bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience. Job Description: The University of Florida's Office of the University Registrar is seeking a University Registrar Services Coordinator III to support the administration, maintenance, and enhancement of the university's degree audit systems. Serving in a key functional role, this position develops, updates, tests, and maintains degree audit requirements for undergraduate academic programs, ensuring curriculum, academic policies, and program changes are accurately reflected in audit tools that support student degree progress and academic advising. In addition to its primary focus on degree audit administration, the position supports curriculum implementation, degree certification activities, and other academic systems initiatives that contribute to student success and the integrity of the university's academic records. Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Degree Audit & Academic Records Maintain, test, and update undergraduate degree audit requirements within Campus Solutions and Stellic to ensure alignment with approved curricula, academic policies, and degree requirements. Review approved curriculum changes and implement corresponding updates to degree audit configurations and rules. Analyze and resolve degree audit discrepancies, conduct quality assurance reviews, and maintain documentation of audit requirements and processes. Support degree certification activities by reviewing degree requirements and assisting with the accurate and timely conferral of degrees. Serve as a resource to academic advisors and campus partners by providing guidance, troubleshooting support, and training on degree audit functionality and related processes. Collaborate with academic units and other stakeholders to enhance degree audit processes and support student success initiatives. Catalog, Curriculum & Alternative Credentials Support university catalog maintenance and publication activities by implementing approved curriculum changes and ensuring academic program, policy, and requirement information is accurate across the catalog and related systems. Support Comprehensive Learner Record (CLR), digital badge, and alternative credential initiatives through record maintenance, system updates, credential processing, and stakeholder coordination. Provide guidance on catalog, curriculum, CLR, and alternative credential processes, while maintaining related documentation, resources, and procedures. Systems, Testing & Training Assist with testing and validation of updates and enhancements to Registrar Services systems. Troubleshoot system and data issues and assist with identifying appropriate solutions. Maintain process documentation and training resources and provide functional support to campus partners. Special Projects & Other Duties Participate in special projects and process improvement initiatives. Assist with reporting, data review, and documentation of office processes. Support improvements that increase the efficiency and accuracy of Registrar Services operations. Cross-train in related Registrar Services functions to provide support during peak workload periods. Perform other related duties and responsibilities as assigned. Expected Salary: $52,000 In addition, UF offers the following exceptional benefits: Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance State Retirement Plans Paid Time Off (approximately 22 days of vacation leave, 13 days of sick leave, and 11 paid holidays annually) Tuition Assistance (UF Employee Education Program) Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Eligible Employer For more information on benefits, please visit UFHR Benefits and Rewards (ufl.edu) Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in an appropriate area; or a bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience. Preferred: Experience working in a registrar’s office, academic affairs, curriculum management, academic advising, or a related higher education environment. Experience with degree audit, curriculum management, catalog, student information, or credentialing systems. Knowledge of academic policies, curriculum processes, degree requirements, and degree certification practices. Demonstrated ability to interpret and translate complex academic requirements and policies into system configurations and business processes. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, including experience identifying discrepancies, troubleshooting system or data issues, and developing effective solutions. Demonstrated attention to detail and commitment to accuracy and data integrity. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Experience developing process documentation, training materials, or user resources. Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants must upload the following documents to be considered for the position: Cover Letter Resume List of References Applications must be submitted by 11:55p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 13 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541629/animal-care-technician-ii": {
      "title": "Animal Care Technician II",
      "description": "Animal Care Technician II Apply now Job no: 541629 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Veteran's Preference Eligible, Veterinary Medicine/Animal Care Department: 11800000 - RE-ANIMAL CARE SERVICES Classification Title: Animal Care Technician II Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience; or certification as Assistant Laboratory Animal Technician by the American Association for Laboratory Animal Science. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Maintains a valid state driver’s license. Job Description: Responsible for carrying out the Animal Care Services' (ACS) directives and SOPs as governed by the Animal Welfare Act and all applicable rules, regulations and professional standards. Provides more complex animal caretaking duties and begins to specialize in the care of individual species or specialty sections. Completes animal care and cage wash activities as directed by Operations Manager or their designee. Performs duties of Animal Care Technician 1. All actions are completed by strictly and consistently following applicable ACS SOPs including IACUC and EHS safety procedures and policies. Reports any suspected or actual deviations to SOPs or non-routine situations immediately to Operations Manager or their designee When performing husbandry duties, will change cages and racks as scheduled, observes and reports animals for signs of illness, injury, and physical or behavioral changes. Under supervision, performs euthanasia of rodents using carbon dioxide with approved alternate secondary method. Observes, documents, and reports changes in environmental parameters outside acceptable ranges, e.g. temperature, humidity, lighting, etc. Restrains and handles animals for treatment. Sanitizes equipment and animal holding facilities. Ensures housing and environmental compliance with the \"NIH Guide for the Care and Use of Laboratory Animals, Maintains supply stock in all assigned rooms for daily use of investigative staff. Follows established procedures to minimize contamination and insure optimum results for researchers. Observes animals; recognizes and report early manifestations of disease such as labored breathing, lethargy, sores, and dehydration. Restrains animals for examination for injection; collects urine and/or fecal samples as directed by veterinary staff. Collects specimens for clinical analysis and obtains vital signs as directed by veterinary staff. Collects specimens for clinical analysis and obtains vital signs as directed by veterinary staff. Monitors health status of postsurgical and experimental animals. May provide assistance to researchers. When working in cage wash section will operate washers, autoclaves, water bottle fill stations and perform preventative maintenance tasks (i.e. jets are cleaned and sump tanks emptied daily) outlined in cage wash maintenance sheet on main area door. Will perform routine start-up and shut down procedures of equipment as outlined in SOP’s. Ensure equipment being processed is in optimal condition and removed from circulation if damaged or worn. Perform scheduled quality control tests of equipment and submit samples (biological indicators, water sample etc.) to ACS diagnostic lab for processing. Will assist in receiving and rotating feed and supplies. Transports caging supplies between animal rooms and cage washrooms. Will sanitize cage washing rooms and other support areas, such as hallways and storage rooms May provide guidance, instruction and direction to ACTI staff following directives provided by facility supervisor/manager. May be part of the training program for all new staff and provide input and updates to facility manager. Will be required to keep up to date on SOP’s in Policy Manger and input time worked in Time Clock Plus using facility computers during normal working hours. Ensure that leave requests, overtime requests and weekend change requests are submitted timely to area supervisor/manager. Other duties as assigned Expected Salary: $18.00/hr Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience; or certification as Assistant Laboratory Animal Technician by the American Association for Laboratory Animal Science. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Maintains a valid state driver’s license. Preferred: Prefer HS degree or higher with at least 3 years’ experience with research animal care at a research institution or other appropriate environment. AALAS LAT certification at time of hire or within 12 months of hire. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, applicants must provide a cover letter, resume, and list of professional references. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This is not a remote position and is located on the University of Florida main campus in Gainesville, FL. A criminal background check is required. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 20 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541630/administrative-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant II Apply now Job no: 541630 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Human Resources, Veteran's Preference Eligible Department: 26030100 - HH-APK-ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: Administrative Assistant II Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent and four years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Department HR • Prepare and review the submission and approval of human resources transactions, including recruitment, hires, position updates and reclassifications, terminations, and additional pay, etc. Work with college HR Manager as needed on more complex transactions such as Special Pay Increases, retirement, and leave cash outs. • Facilitate faculty votes, including communication and follow up on outcomes • Prepare and support visa and immigration for short and long-term visiting scholars without pay. • Prepare and support visa and immigration related to HR positions, sponsorship of exchange visitors, temporary workers and employment-based permanent residents. Responsible for processing renewal documents for current employees. • Serves as liaison between the unit and Human Resource Services, Academic Personnel, Payroll, Purchasing Services, Disbursement Services or General Accounting. • Attend college and university meetings to ensure the Department’s understanding of and compliance with rules and regulations. Administrative Support • Process travel and expense reports • Provide general administrative assistance, including preparing reports, assisting with special projects, and ensuring smooth daily operations of the department. • Provide support to fiscal staff in the analysis, reconciliation, and approval of Department related Marketplace and Pcard transactions, as well as journal entries. • Assist with reviews of expenditures, balances, and transactional detail. • Support department by answering phones, greeting visitors, distributing incoming/outgoing mail, scheduling of conference rooms, etc. Payroll • Responsible for Payroll processes including communication of payroll closing deadlines, submission of bi-weekly, supplemental, and one-time payments as well as over-payments and refunds. Compiles and analyzes payroll data and compiles reports as needed. • Research and resolve payroll related issues in conjunction with Office Manager and Research Administrator as needed. • Process payroll distributions (including cross-college requests), tuition waivers, and related documentation with assistance from Office Manager and Research Administrator. Manage fellowships, graduate scholarships, and ensure all forms, evaluations, and compliance materials are up to date. Effort • Complete online Effort Reporting and Faculty Assignment reports each semester, working directly with College and Department Research staff, Office Manager and/or faculty members to resolve problems. Expected Salary: Commensurate with experience Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and four years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Proven ability to quickly learn and adapt to new systems, software tools, and processes. Flexibility in adapting to evolving programs and procedures while maintaining a high level of accuracy and efficiency. Experience in a human resources setting is preferred. A customer-focused approach when assisting employees and supervisors, with the ability to handle inquiries professionally and courteously. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to tailor messages thoughtfully and effectively to staff, faculty, supervisors, senior leaders, and other stakeholders.\" A collaborative mindset, working closely with faculty, staff, department administrators, and key stakeholders. A self-motivated, proactive approach to handling responsibilities, problem-solving, and completing assignments. Exceptional attention to detail and a high level of accuracy in all tasks. Excellent organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritize effectively. Strong time management skills to meet deadlines and ensure timely completion of duties. Proficiency in relevant software tools, including Microsoft 365/Office Suite (Word, PowerPoint, Excel, OneNote, Teams), Dropbox, and DocuSign. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered for this position, please upload a cover letter and resume. This position is only open to current UF staff. Monday-Friday, 8:00 am – 5:00 pm This position is expected to work in the office on UF main campus Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 13 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
