    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541631/extension-program-manager-efnep-orange-county": {
      "title": "Extension Program Manager - EFNEP Orange County",
      "description": "Extension Program Manager - EFNEP Orange County Apply now Job no: 541631 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Orange Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Agricultural Sciences Department: 60450000 - AG-EXPANDED NUTRITION PROGRAM Classification Title: Extension Program Manager Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Administration and Reporting Stay up to date with UF/IFAS Extension EFNEP requirements, policies, and guidance, and provide staff with timely updates and clarification as needed. Engage in EFNEP and county trainings, meetings and professional development to support effective program implementation and coordination. Complete required programmatic reports accurately and on time, including success stories and activity reports as requested. Develop and administer county needs assessment program plan in alignment with program goals and funding requirements. Monitor progress toward county program goals and address areas needing improvement. Maintain the integrity, accuracy, and completeness of program records. Review and approve staff administrative records, including travel expenses, grocery receipts, work logs/calendars, and time and leave, in accordance with UF and program requirements. Procure program supplies and materials within budgetary guidelines and maintain accountability for program assets. Delegate appropriate administrative and reporting responsibilities to the Office Assistant and provide necessary oversight. Team Leadership, Training and Performance Management Supervise and provide day-to-day leadership to assigned EFNEP staff. Hold regular team meetings and individual check-ins to communicate expectations, address needs, and support staff performance. Coach and mentor employees to strengthen performance, professional skills, and achievement of program expectations, including caseload goals. Address employee relations and performance concerns promptly and complete required UF performance management processes. Observe each Nutrition Educator conducting an educational session at least twice per year, including one observation of participant evaluation administration; document observations and review feedback with the employee to identify strengths and areas for growth. Conduct independent follow-up with participants or community partners, as appropriate, to assess and address significant program implementation or performance concerns. Coordinate with the EFNEP state office to fill vacancies, including participating in candidate selection and providing onboarding and orientation for new hires. Plan and deliver group and individual staff training on nutrition content, curricula, teaching techniques, recruitment, and other required competencies. Provide group training one to two times per month and identify appropriate topics and resources for staff self-study. As applicable, obtain ServSafe® Food Protection Manager certification, coordinate SafeStaff® Food Handler certification for staff, and ensure appropriate food-handling practices at EFNEP offices and programming sites. Program Promotion and Recruitment Maintain existing community partnerships and develop new partnerships that support EFNEP programming and participant recruitment. Identify and recruit appropriate teaching sites in collaboration with EFNEP staff, the County Extension Director, and other partners. Promote EFNEP within the community to increase awareness of and access to program services. Participate in community advisory groups, coalitions, and other meetings that support program outreach, recruitment, and partnership development. Support Public Health and Policy, Systems, and Environmental (PSE) Approaches Maintain existing community partnerships and develop new partnerships that support EFNEP programming and participant recruitment. Identify and recruit appropriate teaching sites in collaboration with EFNEP staff, the County Extension Director, and other partners. Promote EFNEP within the community to increase awareness of and access to program services. Participate in community advisory groups, coalitions, and other meetings that support program outreach, recruitment, and partnership development. Travel Travel independently throughout the assigned county or geographic area to support staff supervision and program operations, including site visits, teaching observations, and meetings with partners, advisory groups, and Extension personnel. Travel outside assigned county or geographic area for UF/IFAS Extension EFNEP meetings, trainings, and other program responsibilities. Complete overnight travel as required for annual training and other program-related activities. Driver’s license is required for this position. Expected Salary: $61,000 annually The University of Florida offers highly competitive benefits and retirement options, generous leave plans, a health and wellness program that reflects its commitment to qualify of work, and many more competitive perks and rewards. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Valid driver's license and reliable daily transportation Preferred: Demonstrated ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment and initiative, manage competing priorities, solve problems effectively, and complete responsibilities with minimal day-to-day supervision. Strong leadership and supervisory experience, including setting expectations, managing employee performance, coaching and developing staff, fostering accountability, and creating a positive and productive team environment. Strong background in nutrition, community nutrition, public health nutrition, or a closely related field. Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN) and/or Licensed Dietitian/Nutritionist (LD/N) credential strongly preferred. Excellent organizational, written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, including the ability to coordinate multiple activities, communicate effectively with diverse audiences, and develop and deliver engaging presentations and trainings. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain collaborative, productive working relationships with staff, Extension colleagues, community partners, and other stakeholders. Background check required. Attached: EFNEP Extension Program Manager - Full Position Description.pdf Attached: EFNEP Core Values.pdf Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, please attach to the application: Resume Cover letter articulating why you are a good fit for this position. 3 references with contact information and relationship to applicant Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This is a time-limited, grant funded position in EFNEP Orange County Extension office. For inquiries or questions, please contact: Genena Blanchette at genena@ufl.edu Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 28 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541634/ops-research-coordinator": {
      "title": "OPS Research Coordinator",
      "description": "OPS Research Coordinator Apply now Job no: 541634 Work type: Temp Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Health Care Administration/Support Department: 29050300 - MD-RHEUMATOLOGY Classification Title: OPS Research Coordinator Classification Minimum Requirements: High School Diploma or equivalent. Job Description: • Assist with coordination and implementation of clinical research studies within Dr. Ronald Staud’s laboratory. • Assist with participant screening, recruitment, enrollment, scheduling, and follow up activities. • Support informed consent activities in accordance with approved study protocols and institutional requirements. • Coordinate and support research visits, study procedures, and collection of research data and specimens. • Maintain accurate and complete study documentation, source records, case report forms, and electronic databases. • Enter research data and assist with responding to data queries and maintaining data quality. • Assist with IRB submissions, amendments, continuing reviews, regulatory documentation, and maintenance of essential study files. • Follow approved research protocols, institutional policies, Good Clinical Practice requirements, and applicable regulatory requirements. • Work closely with the current Clinical Research Coordinator to learn established study workflows, protocols, systems, and laboratory procedures. • Participate in structured cross training and knowledge transfer to develop competency in critical research responsibilities and ensure continuity of study operations. • Provide research coordination coverage and operational support as competency is established. • Assist with study monitoring, audits, study initiation, closeout, and other research activities as assigned. • Communicate effectively with the Principal Investigator, research staff, clinical personnel, study participants, and other research partners. • Perform other duties related to clinical research activities as assigned. Expected Salary: $15.00 to $20.00 Hourly Required Qualifications: Associate’s degree or an allied health professional degree in an appropriate area and one year of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Experience and/or certification in phlebotomy. Special Instructions to Applicants: Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 20 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541635/senior-copywriter-enrollment-marketing-communications": {
      "title": "Senior Copywriter (Enrollment Marketing & Communications)",
      "description": "Senior Copywriter (Enrollment Marketing & Communications) Apply now Job no: 541635 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Communications/Public Relations/Marketing Department: 03010300 - EM-ADMIN PUBLICATIONS-COMMUNIC Classification Title: Writer Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area; or an associate’s degree and two years of relevant experience. Job Description: The University of Florida’s Division of Enrollment Management is seeking a talented and strategic Senior Copywriter to create compelling, audience focused content that supports student recruitment, enrollment, and engagement initiatives. In this role, you will develop impactful copy across a variety of channels, including email campaigns, websites, marketing materials, digital advertising, video scripts, newsletters, and other communications. Working closely with subject matter experts, designers, and marketing professionals, you will translate complex information into clear, engaging content while maintaining university brand and editorial standards. The ideal candidate is a skilled storyteller with exceptional writing, editing, and proofreading abilities, experience developing SEO focused web content, and a data informed approach to enhancing message effectiveness. This position offers an opportunity to shape the voice of Enrollment Management and contribute to strategic marketing campaigns that connect with prospective and current students. Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Copywriting & Content Development Develop engaging, impactful, and audience focused content across a variety of channels, including email campaigns, websites, marketing collateral, digital advertising, newsletters, annual reports, press releases, video scripts, and other communications. Write, edit, and refine content that supports student recruitment, enrollment, retention, and engagement initiatives while maintaining university brand standards, editorial guidelines, and a consistent voice. Translate complex academic, administrative, and technical information into clear, compelling, and user-friendly content tailored to diverse audiences. Create content that aligns with strategic communication goals, campaign objectives, and audience needs across print and digital platforms. Proofread and edit content to ensure accuracy, clarity, consistency, quality, and adherence to established style standards. Review and provide editorial feedback on content developed by colleagues and stakeholders to ensure messaging effectiveness and brand alignment. Content Strategy & Collaboration Conduct research to support content development and ensure messaging is accurate, relevant, and aligned with communication goals. Collaborate with campus stakeholders to develop engaging content with a consistent and cohesive voice. Develop and optimize web content using SEO best practices to support visibility, readability, and engagement. Review and refine existing content to improve readability, accuracy, voice, and overall effectiveness. Content Performance & Insights Use data, surveys, and communication results to evaluate message effectiveness and user satisfaction. Identify opportunities to improve content based on communication performance and results. Apply findings to future content development and communication strategies. Campaign Support Assist with documenting communication campaigns and mapping communication flows. Support testing and review of customized communication campaigns. Collaborate with the Email Marketing Specialist to support accurate and effective campaign delivery. Other Duties Perform other related duties and responsibilities as assigned. Expected Salary: $65,000 In addition, UF offers the following exceptional benefits: Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance State Retirement Plans Paid Time Off (approximately 22 days of vacation leave, 13 days of sick leave, and 11 paid holidays annually) Tuition Assistance (UF Employee Education Program) Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Eligible Employer For more information on benefits, please visit UFHR Benefits and Rewards (ufl.edu) Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area; or an associate’s degree and two years of relevant experience. Preferred: Five years of professional writing and communications experience in higher education, publishing, an agency setting, or a related professional environment. Strong writing, editing, proofreading, and storytelling skills. Strong written and verbal communication skills and demonstrated problem solving abilities. Ability to be resourceful and proactive while seeking assistance when appropriate. Excellent attention to detail, accuracy, organization, and time management skills. Experience developing content across multiple platforms and communication channels. Demonstrated ability to translate complex information into clear, engaging, and effective messaging. Experience collaborating with stakeholders to develop communication and marketing content. Knowledge of brand and editorial standards and content development best practices. Experience developing web content and applying SEO principles. Ability to use research, data, and communication results to improve communication effectiveness. Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants must upload the following documents to be considered for the position: Cover Letter Resume List of References Applications must be submitted by 11:55p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 20 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
