    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541491/recsports-student-assistant-lake-wauburg-waterfront-lifeguard": {
      "title": "RecSports Student Assistant - Lake Wauburg Waterfront Lifeguard",
      "description": "RecSports Student Assistant - Lake Wauburg Waterfront Lifeguard Apply now Job no: 541491 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Recreation/Event Services, Student Services Department: 04020100 - SL-RECSPTS ADMIN Classification Title: STU-AST-NON-CLERICAL & ADMIN Job Description: The Department of Recreational Sports is currently looking for Lake Wauburg Lifeguards to join our energetic team and move Gators toward lifelong wellbeing! Lifeguards serve the department by overseeing water-based activities while ensuring the safety of our members and guests. Duties also include monitoring boaters on the lake, operating a motorized rescue boat, and assisting with equipment rentals at the boathouse. Successful candidates will begin work at the start of Spring 2027. For more information, contact Brent Gibson at brent.gibson@ufl.edu . For more information about the role and onboarding process, visit RecSports Student Employment Webpage . RecSports Team Member Responsibilities Develop professional relationships with co-workers, participants, and guests. Uphold and exceed the expectations of the Cornerstones of RecSports Service: accountability, anticipating needs, attitude, and atmosphere. Demonstrate a desire to learn and apply knowledge as a RecSports ambassador. Take ownership of RecSports facilities and programs by exhibiting a responsible work ethic. Promote and maintain cleanliness and appearance within and surrounding RecSports facilities. Enforce RecSports policies and procedures to promote participant safety and satisfaction. Respond to all emergency situations and adhere to established protocol including pre- and post- incident procedures. All RecSports employees are expected to abide by the RecSports Student Staff Career Readiness Principles that clarifies shared expectations and standards in effort to best serve our patrons, develop each team member, and prepare student employees for future career endeavors. Job Position Responsibilities Perform all necessary lifeguarding, First Aid, and CPR skills in accordance with American Red Cross certification standards. Monitor the safety of swimmers and boaters on the lake. Perform appropriate saves and rescues for swimmers or boaters as needed. Prevent injuries by identifying and addressing hazardous situations and behaviors. Observe and enforce facility rules, regulations, and policies. Operate the rescue boat and conduct Lake Watch as assigned. Maintain a current Florida Boater Safety Education ID Card to operate the rescue boat for Lake Watch. Provide customer service and safety briefings for patrons renting boats and equipment. Assist patrons with launching boats into the lake. Obtain working knowledge of Hobie Cat Wave sailboats through internal training. Answer incoming phone calls and provide information about hours of operation, areas of interest, reservation policies, and special events. Support Lake Wauburg special events and facility reservations. Perform routine maintenance and cleaning, including maintaining restrooms, emptying trash, and restocking supplies. Participate in departmental and unit-specific training, including mandatory fall training and monthly meetings/in-services. Assist supervisors and professional staff with additional duties as assigned. RecSports Fall Kick-Off 2027: Tuesday, August 17th 8am – 9:30am Fall Kick-Off is our all-staff event to discuss department-wide updates, facilitate unit training sessions, as well as cultivate community and positive energy within our RecSports team. All RecSports Student Staff are expected to attend and will be paid for their training time. Expected Salary: $16.25 per hour Required Qualifications: Requirements/Qualifications Successfully complete a Lifeguard Try-Out (pre-employment water test). Reliable transportation to and from Lake Wauburg. A valid driver’s license. Valid American Red Cross Lifeguard/CPR/AED/First Aid Certification or the ability to obtain certification by start of employment. Availability to work 7–15 hours per week during operating hours, including weekdays, weekends, and potentially academic breaks. Ability to attend mandatory staff meetings and in-service training. This position is open to all students who are eligible to work on campus and will be employed through student Other Personnel Services (OPS) and must maintain a minimum 2.0 grade point average. Registered students are employed on a part-time basis, up to 20 hours per week. *Federal Work Study students are encouraged to apply! Preferred: Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in customer service, working at a waterfront or recreational facility. Special Instructions to Applicants: *All applicants must register for and attend one Lifeguard Try-Out to be considered for the position. This is a time-limited position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Questions: Contact Brent Gibson, brent.gibson@ufl.edu . Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 04 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 25 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541492/recsports-student-assistant-lake-wauburg-challenge-course-facillitator": {
      "title": "RecSports Student Assistant - Lake Wauburg Challenge Course Facillitator",
      "description": "RecSports Student Assistant - Lake Wauburg Challenge Course Facillitator Apply now Job no: 541492 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Recreation/Event Services, Student Services Department: 04020100 - SL-RECSPTS ADMIN Classification Title: STU-AST-NON-CLERICAL & ADMIN Job Description: The Department of Recreational Sports is currently looking for Lake Wauburg Challenge Course Facilitators to join our energetic team and move Gators toward lifelong wellbeing! Facilitators serve the department by leading experiential team-building activities on both land and in the air that promote, enhance, and support the development of healthy group relationships. Duties include facilitating low and high ropes course activities, and leading on and off-site programs. Successful candidates will begin work at the start of Spring 2027. For more information, contact Lilly Stevens at lstevens1@ufl.edu . For more information about the role and onboarding process, visit RecSports Student Employment Webpage . RecSports Team Member Responsibilities Develop professional relationships with co-workers, participants, and guests. Uphold and exceed the expectations of the Cornerstones of RecSports Service: accountability, anticipating needs, attitude, and atmosphere. Demonstrate a desire to learn and apply knowledge as a RecSports ambassador. Take ownership of RecSports facilities and programs by exhibiting a responsible work ethic. Promote and maintain cleanliness and appearance within and surrounding RecSports facilities. Enforce RecSports policies and procedures to promote participant safety and satisfaction. Respond to all emergency situations and adhere to established protocol including pre- and post- incident procedures. All RecSports employees are expected to abide by the RecSports Student Staff Career Readiness Principles that clarifies shared expectations and standards in effort to best serve our patrons, develop each team member, and prepare student employees for future career endeavors. Job Position Responsibilities Provide high-quality customer service. Facilitate activities to promote and enhance individual and group teamwork, development, and wellness. Must participate and demonstrate proficient skills in Low and High Course training, including high ropes course rescues. Provide pre-course safety briefings. Assist with set up, take down, opening, closing, cleaning, and other duties as directed. Ability to lead and speak to large groups of people, maintaining professionalism in all situations. Responsible for consistent supervision of challenge course participants throughout entire course. Responsible for managing risk and promoting well-being of participants, teammates, and self. Support Lake Wauburg special events and facility reservations. Develop professional relationships with co-workers, participants, and guests. Administer First Aid/CPR/AED in an emergency. Enforce rules, regulations and policies. Inspect facilities and equipment for unsafe conditions, remedy the condition, and or notify supervisors. Participate in departmental and unit training. Assist supervisors and professional staff with additional duties as assigned. RecSports Fall Kick-Off 2027: Tuesday, August 17th 8am – 9:30am Fall Kick-Off is our all-staff event to discuss department-wide updates, facilitate unit training sessions, as well as cultivate community and positive energy within our RecSports team. All RecSports Student Staff are expected to attend and will be paid for their training time. Expected Salary: $15.65 per hour Required Qualifications: Requirements/Qualifications Comfortable working ~30 feet in the air. Reliable transportation to and from Lake Wauburg. A valid driver’s license. Valid First Aid/CPR/AED certification or the ability to obtain certification within the first 30 days of employment. Availability to work 5–12 hours per week during operating hours, including weekdays, weekends, and potentially academic breaks. Ability to attend mandatory staff meetings and in-service training. This position is open to all students who are eligible to work on campus and will be employed through student Other Personnel Services (OPS) and must maintain a minimum 2.0 grade point average. Registered students are employed on a part-time basis, up to 20 hours per week and additional hours with an approved Hours Extension Form. *Federal Work Study students are encouraged to apply. Preferred: Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in customer service. Previous experience facilitating teambuilding, low and high ropes courses. Professional or personal experience climbing and/or belaying. Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants must submit a resume to be considered. For more information, contact Lilly Stevens at lstevens1@ufl.edu . Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This is a time-limited position. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 04 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 25 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
