    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541606/human-resources-generalist-ii": {
      "title": "Human Resources Generalist II",
      "description": "Human Resources Generalist II Apply now Job no: 541606 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Human Resources Department: 29140101 - MD-SURGERY-ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: HR Generalist II Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: The Department of Surgery is seeking highly qualified candidates to provide professional support and expertise in the implementation of a broad range of human resources functions or programs. This position will serve as a human resources business partner to the administration, faculty, and staff of the department of Surgery, which includes the Regional Programs in Daytona and Deltona. Essential functions include recruitment, onboarding, effort reporting, and training coordination. This position requires a thorough knowledge of human resources policies and procedures as well as the hospital credentialing process. Duties include, but are not limited to: Performs broad range of human resources functions including, but not limited to, recruitment and staffing, timekeeping, and promotion and tenure. Recommends policies and operating practices associated with the Surgery Department. Processes all personnel transactions in accordance with University policies and procedures. Performs complex data analysis, prepares reports and/or presentations for management. Monitors the effectiveness of human resources policies and recommends revisions or modification to meet the needs of the university. Serves as a human resources consultant to faculty and staff by providing advice and guidance related to human resources, such as, all personnel issues, including benefits eligibility, extended leave, including FMLA, policies and procedures, etc.. Coordinates and processes extended leaves of absence. Prepares leave accrual projections for those anticipating extended leaves or terminating employment, including obtaining minimal leave required to maintain benefits from Fringe Benefits on employee’s behalf. Maintains and shares as needed all human resources data related to APPs in the department, both UF and Shands employed. Information required includes credentialing, effort allocations between divisions and Shands, multiple employee ID’s and hire and termination dates. Maintains current departmental HR records. Reviews compensation data for accuracy as requested. Maintains departmental personnel files in accordance with University policy. Ensures that all employees participate in required training sessions. Prepares compliance reports. Maintains Faculty Assignment spreadsheets and documentation. Other duties as assigned. Expected Salary: $65,000-$70,000/annually Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Thorough understanding of UF and College of Medicine personnel and payroll policies, procedures and requirements. • Thorough understanding of PeopleSoft’s human resource applications and rules governing each application to timely process faculty and staff recruitments, job actions, position actions, compliance reporting, national and local advertising, and effort tracking. • Strong ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing to independently generate internal and external correspondence and advertisements. • Proven track record in recruitment, particularly faculty recruitment. • Advanced computer skills in Microsoft Word and Excel to prepare spreadsheets and other documents as needed. • Strong organizational skills • Strong attention to details. • Strong ability to prioritize job assignments to complete within established time limits. • Strong customer service skills. • Strong ability to generate and analyze payroll and HR reports.Item two Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter, resume, and a minimum of three professional references with contact information. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/537351/treatment-plant-opr-entry": {
      "title": "Treatment Plant Opr - Entry",
      "description": "Treatment Plant Opr - Entry Apply now Job no: 537351 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Facilities Operations/Skilled Trades, Veteran's Preference Eligible Department: 63700700 - FS-UTILITIES-WASTE WATER Classification Title: Treatment Plant Opr - Entry Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent. Must obtain a class C wastewater operator's certificate in accordance with Florida Statutes 403.101 and 468.540 552 and Regulation 61E1241, F.A.C. within two years of employment. Job Description: Learns and assist to operate the Water Reclamation Plant in a safe and efficient manner, keeping in compliance with all existing requirements and published operational procedures. Learns and assist to record all required instrumentation readings, review data and take corrective action based on analysis of it. Learns and assist to operate sludge de-watering equipment. Performs routine cleaning of all buildings, rinses down all tanks and flumes and vacuums chlorine contact chambers Learns and assist to perform required laboratory analysis and takes corrective action based on laboratory tests. Learns and assist to monitor the operational status of all equipment. Learns and assist to shift from automatic operational mode to the manual mode as necessary. Learns and assist to perform required checkout procedures, re-calibrations and transfer system from manual mode to operational mode Learns and assist to make adjustment to equipment as required. Learns and assist to maintain plant operational and security status weekends, holidays and after normal working hours. Learns and assist to maintain daily records Learns and assist plant mechanics and perform preventive maintenance as needed. Proof of a State of Florida Class E operator’s license required. Class “C” Wastewater License must be obtained by the end of the eighteen (18) months of employment. The costs of all books and instructions including one test will be paid by the University. NORMAL WORK SCHEDULE: Daily from 7:00 a.m. to 3:30 p.m. during initial training period for 6 months, then transition to evenings from 4:00 p.m. to 12:00 a.m., total hours per week: 40 Expected Salary: $16.00 to $17.00 Hourly Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent. Must obtain a class C wastewater operator's certificate in accordance with Florida Statutes 403.101 and 468.540 552 and Regulation 61E1241, F.A.C. within two years of employment. Preferred: KNOWLEDGE OF: Learn advanced waste water treatment principles, use of hand tools, computer use and safety rules. LEARN SKILLS IN: Chemistry, biology, mechanical working, and process control ABILITY TO: Learn to operate plant with minor supervision, interpret results of process control tests and adjust plant accordingly, maintain proper log sheets, and communicate with preceding and following shift workers. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 15 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/539795/fire-safety-coordinator": {
      "title": "Fire Safety Coordinator",
      "description": "Fire Safety Coordinator Apply now Job no: 539795 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Facilities Operations/Skilled Trades, Environmental/Occupational Safety Department: 71010000 - EHS-ENVR - HLTH - SAFETY-ADMIN Classification Title: Fire Safety Coordinator Classification Minimum Requirements: Associate in Science degree in Fire Science Technology and two (2) years of responsible experience with a governmental agency or private organization, including enforcement or design work to meet required fire regulations, fire prevention inspections or development, and fire plan check or design of fire systems, or 10 years as a Fire Marshal with a local municipality or state agency. Must be certified as a Fire Safety Inspector 1 in accordance with Florida Statute 633. Job Description: Inspects UF Buildings, Fraternities and Sororities for Fire Code Compliance and prepares reports to be submitted for correction of code violations. Reviews Fire Alarm Activity Logs to ensure proper maintenance of fire alarm systems in accordance with UF’s False Alarm Reduction program Supervises and assists with the Enhanced Radio System monitoring of all campus buildings. Provides assistance and oversight to the inspections of fire safety related items in new construction projects. Conducts public outreach for fire safety including providing fire extinguisher use training. Other duties as assigned. Must have a valid Florida Driver’s License. This position requires a post offer health assessment. Must be certified as a Fire Safety Inspector 1 in accordance with Florida Statute 633. This position is designated as an Essential Employee for the University, as the employee’s response immediately following an emergency event in which the continuation of critical and essential services is needed. NORMAL WORK SCHEDULE: Monday – Friday, 8 AM to 5 PM, or as approved by supervisor. 40 hours per week Occasional travel to offsite locations. Expected Salary: Commensurate with Education & Experience Required Qualifications: Associate in science degree in Fire Science Technology and two (2) years of responsible experience with a governmental agency or private organization, including enforcement or design work to meet required fire regulations, fire prevention inspections or development, and fire plan check or design of fire systems, or 10 years as a Fire Marshal with a local municipality or state agency. Must be certified as a Fire Safety Inspector 1 in accordance with Florida Statute 633. Preferred: EDUCATION & TRAINNG: Bachelor’s degree in engineering, Architecture, Building Construction or Business Administration. NICET certification. EXPERIENCE: Five years supervisory experience. KNOWLEDGE: A thorough knowledge of the standard fire codes, blueprint reading and interpretation, construction terminology and techniques. SKILLS: Excellent written and oral communication skills. ABILITIES: Ability to interface with professionals such as architects, engineers, and construction workers. Ability to work with database reporting systems to ensure compliance with required codes. PHYSICAL QUALIFICATIONS: Repeated bending Climbing Areas of excessive noise Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 15 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
