    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/540183/administrative-spec-ii": {
      "title": "Administrative Spec II",
      "description": "Administrative Spec II Apply now Job no: 540183 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Transportation Services Department: 68040000 - BS-TRANSPORTATION - PARKING Classification Title: Administrative Spec II Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree and three years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Administrative Support: - Provides high-level administrative assistance to the Senior (Sr.) Director of TAPS and three Associate Directors, including calendar management, meeting coordination, and preparation of confidential reports and correspondence. - Manages routine and non-routine tasks that support the daily operations of TAPS. - Assists in preparing presentations, reports, and documentation for leadership meetings. -Ensures that time and leave are reported timely and accurately as required for UF Payroll deadlines. -Assists the BA-HR office in preparing all documents for leave of absences. Operational Support - Assists with managing validator lists for gate systems and runs monthly report on validations. - Assists with managing office supply inventory, ordering items as needed. - Assists with Preview and represents TAPS with campus events. - Manages the TAPS website, periodically verifying current information and posting website updates. - Tracks and logs departmental complaints/inquiries to ensure timely responses and closeout. Personnel Responsibilities: - Acts as liaison between TAPS and the Business Affairs | Construction, Facilities & Real Estate Human Resources (BA | CFRE HR) office. department. - Assists the BA | CFRE HR office in competing all personnel-related actions, including posting new positions for hire, updating position descriptions, new hire paperwork, separations, Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) actions, and leave administration. - Manages user log-ins for TAPS employees on various software platforms. - Assigns training for new hires within TAPS, tracks completion. - Maintains current general knowledge of UF personnel policies and procedures. Additional duties as assigned. Valid FL Driver's License is Required. NORMAL WORK SCHEDULE: Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm 40 Hours per week Expected Salary: $53,000.00 Annually may exceed based on experience. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and three years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: KNOWLEDGE: - Proficient knowledge in Microsoft Office Suite (Outlook, Word, Excel) - Knowledge of PeopleSoft System - Knowledge of UF Financial System, or in producing travel authorizations and expense reports. - Knowledge of standard business formats and styles for letters, business forms and reports. - Knowledge of general office procedures, techniques necessary for handling telephone calls in a courtesy and efficient manner, basic filing practices, and basic record retention requirements. - Knowledge rules and regulations governing Payroll and Leave Administration systems, and UF administrative principles and procedures ABILITIES: - Ability to work independently and use a personal computer in a productive manner. - Ability to organize and coordinate work assignments to meet deadlines. - Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. - Ability to establish and maintain positive working relationship with co-workers and extended campus personnel. - Ability to perform duties in an accurate, timely and confidential manner. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Position has been reposted, previous applicants still under consideration. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 15 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
